Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight One-Shot Activation Ceremony P0 Requirements Analysis

@ [analysis_uuid] c0e047f0-560e-4e7f-b69c-8cc8ce4136d1
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] e4929ffa-1c10-451e-ad4d-ddbccc992c52

& [RequiredMeaning]
  + one ceremony instance must bind one exact published runner lineage and one exact producer plan
  + proposal compilation and lineage verification are deterministic provider-free operations
  + an authorize or reject decision must be externally supplied by the named operator and independently admitted without inference from prose progress or publication
  + authorization is finite by ceremony UUID nonce time interval attempt count permit count process count and exact effect ceiling
  + a private non-cloneable permit is minted only for admitted authorize and is consumed before the physical runner boundary
  + every failure refusal expiration drift replay or ambiguity closes the instance with no retry
  + successful process output is not completion until the runner receipt is independently replayed and a terminal record closes the instance

& [RequiredProof]
  + exact lineage profiles shapes order edges authority transitions and strict canonical digest rules
  + adversaries for decision inference stale decision replay substitution permit reuse post-consumption failure receipt tamper and effect widening
  + formation verification under both PowerShell generations with zero provider requests remote calls effects and runner invocations

& [Deferred]
  + implementation permit minting live operator-decision capture executable observation invocation receipt persistence and remote preflight remain later separately governed phases
